{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And to the children of Levi.</b> Since we find regarding the priesthood (Numbers 5) ״והיתה לו ולזרעו אחריו״ — and it shall be his and his seed after him — meaning that the priesthood extends to the seed of Aaron forever, generation after generation, but regarding the Levitical service we do not find the expression 'after him,' and if so, from where do we know that the Levitical service extends forever like the priesthood? Therefore Scripture says ולבני לוי — 'and to the children of Levi' — and the vav adds to the preceding matter: just as the priesthood is forever, for thus it mentioned above concerning it ״חק עולם ברית מלח״ — an everlasting statute, a covenant of salt — so too the Levitical service is an everlasting statute, a covenant of salt. And in these sections the priesthood and the Levitical service were established for the seed of Aaron, after the challengers were judged and caught in the snare of their own deeds and fell from their own counsels; and because of this the blossoming of the staff was a sign, as it is written (Numbers 17:23): ״פרח מטה אהרן לבית לוי״ — the staff of Aaron for the house of Levi blossomed — as I mentioned above. And the blossoming is a sign of swiftness and the sprouting of calamity for every challenger, just as we find with Uzziah (2 Chronicles 26). And so we find in Scripture that blossoming is a sign of swiftness, whether for calamity or for reward — for calamity, as it is written (Psalms 92): ״בפרוח רשעים כמו עשב״ — when the wicked flourish like grass; for reward, as is said concerning the time of redemption (Isaiah 35:1–2): ״פרוח תפרח ותגל אף גילת ורנן כבוד הלבנון נתן לה הדר הכרמל והשרון המה יראו כבוד ה׳ הדר אלהינו״, and it is written (Hosea 14:6): ״אהיה כטל לישראל יפרח כשושנה ויך שרשיו כלבנון״, and so Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Proverbs 11:28): ״וכעלה צדיקים יפרחו״, and so his father David, peace be upon him, said (Psalms 92:13–14): ״צדיק כתמר יפרח כארז בלבנון ישגה שתולים בבית ה׳ בחצרות אלהינו יפריחו״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:56.834943715Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}